    { n: 3, t: "Pick a workaround", time: "45 min", body: "The documented fixes are all hacks: a <strong>Boolean-Toggle</strong> (flip a 'renewal created' flag, wait 31 minutes for the re-enrollment buffer, reset it on the new deal), a <strong>dual odd/even-year workflow</strong> pattern, or a per-year dropdown with one branch each." },
    { n: 4, t: "Keep forecasts honest", time: "10 min", body: "Exclude multi-year deals from near-term forecasts by filtering on Renewal Date, or they inflate the pipeline for quarters they will not actually close in." },
  ],
  burden: "The 31-minute buffer and odd/even contortions exist only to work around a HubSpot platform limit. They are brittle, painful to test (you wait 31 minutes between each simulated close), and a single mis-set flag silently breaks the chain at year 2 or spawns duplicates. There is no first-class 'here is this customer's renewal ladder' view, you reconstruct it by hopping Original Deal IDs.",
  bridge: "The build tracks the chain in a real parent-child ledger and creates each renewal <strong>server-side, outside HubSpot's workflow enrollment</strong>, so the 31-minute and odd/even hacks are unnecessary and year 3 and beyond never stall. The audit tells you which of your chains are set to break, before they do.",
